# Minimal agent profile (PROFILE=minimal): lean headless box for AI agents.
# Shell + core dev toolchain only — no GUI, no desktop/locale/IME, no GUI
# editors (VSCodium/Cursor are skipped in step 20 too; Docker is kept there).
# Hand-curated, like apt.list — which keeps the SHAPE of an `apt-mark
# showmanual` dump but is maintained by hand too (there is no exporter any
# more). Step 10 still applies its boot/kernel/third-party filters on top of
# both, harmlessly.
build-essential
ca-certificates
curl
git
gpg
# ── terminfo for INBOUND ssh ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Not for terminals on THIS box — for the terminal on the other end. ssh
# forwards TERM and not the terminfo, so a client running kitty/alacritty/
# wezterm/foot answers "unknown terminal type" here unless the entry exists
# locally. That is true of every box this repo builds, at every profile, and it
# does not depend on which terminal (if any) is installed here — so it lives at
# the apt layer, unconditional.
#   ncurses-base   (Essential, always present) already covers xterm-256color,
#                  screen-* and tmux-256color.
#   ncurses-term   adds alacritty, wezterm, foot, vte-256color + ~2,900 more.
#   kitty-terminfo adds xterm-kitty, which ncurses-term does NOT carry.
# Ghostty has no entry anywhere in Ubuntu; that one is the client's job
# (`infocmp -x xterm-ghostty | ssh host 'tic -x -'`). See provision/README.md.
kitty-terminfo
ncurses-term
tmux
wget
zsh
zsh-autosuggestions
zsh-syntax-highlighting
